From 9c690d0d31e4c94e784cbb0a048961c6960c6c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristian <kristian@apache.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:47:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Answer Kafka table metadata from the table handle

The INSERT planner takes the columns it writes from the table metadata,
which the Kafka connector still built by describing the table again,
while analysis took them from the table handle. A schema registry based
supplier describes a table with its latest schema versions, so a schema
registered between the two gave the plan columns the handle did not
have, and the pinned data schema did not protect the write.

Carry the column comment in the column handle, the one piece of the
table metadata the handle lacked, and build the table metadata, and the
table schema with it, from the handle. Listing the columns of all tables
still describes each table, as it has no handle.
